from pathlib import Path
import json,hashlib
r=Path('/work/c8-tuning');old=Path('/work/c8-ablation')
entries=[('SWA attention + reduce, 128 KV','attention_t128','attention_paged_128'),('HCA attention + reduce, 136 KV','attention_envelope144_valid136','attention_paged_136'),('HCA attention + reduce, 144 KV','attention_t144','attention_paged_144'),('CSA attention + reduce, 384 KV','attention_envelope640_valid384','attention_paged_384'),('CSA attention + reduce, 512 KV','attention_envelope640_valid512','attention_paged_512'),('CSA attention + reduce, 640 KV','attention_t640','attention_paged_640'),('mHC post + FFN pre/RMSNorm','mhc_post_pre','mhc_native_region'),('Top6 routing + metadata','routing','routing'),('Routed MoE including input quant','routed_moe','routed_moe'),('HCA compressor non-boundary','compress_case1_pos1024','compress_case1_pos1024'),('HCA compressor boundary','compress_case1_pos1535','compress_case1_pos1535'),('Indexer compressor non-boundary','compress_case2_pos1024','compress_case2_pos1024'),('Indexer compressor boundary','compress_case2_pos1535','compress_case2_pos1535')]
rows=[]
for label,ok,nk in entries:
 o=json.loads((old/(ok+'.json')).read_text());n=json.loads((r/'final'/(nk+'.json')).read_text());v=n['rounds'][-1]['median_us'];oldv=o['rounds'][-1]['median_us']['fused']
 rows.append(dict(group=label,native_us=v['native'],before_fused_us=oldv,after_fused_us=v['fused'],vs_native_pct=(v['fused']/v['native']-1)*100,speedup_vs_old=oldv/v['fused'],result='final/'+nk+'.json',validation=n['validation'],kernel_count=n['kernel_count']))
validation={}
for name in ['routing-validation','paged-validation','moe-validation','mhc-validation']:
 validation[name]=json.loads((r/(name+'.json')).read_text())
report=dict(date='2026-10-21',concurrency=8,shape='Flash TP1 1024input/1024output decode shape envelope',status='selected isolated single-launch regions; NOT installed in /work/batch-full or ATOM; NOT a newly validated full-layer/e2e result',method='4 GPUs in parallel; paired native/fused flat HIP graphs; 32 repetitions; 40 alternating samples; second round median only',rows=rows,validation=validation,limitations=['Before column is previous fixed-fixture ablation at corresponding shapes; newly paired native/after columns are the current controlled comparison. Attention new cache is scattered/paged, old cache was compact.','8 splits changes the attention reduction grouping versus native default32. Ragged stress max relative RMS 0.001486 versus default32, <=0.000009887 versus AITER same8 splits. No modelwide accuracy claim.','Native mHC warp-specialized reducer is retained; full-layer embedding can change thread/register/LDS requirements.','HCA compressor subgroup uses a dedicated counter and extra 8x4x3x512 FP32 pooling scratch, only STATE128/R128 boundary alignment tested. Do not share this counter with a 256-CTA barrier.','Routing is learned top6 with optional bias, not hash routing; 64 metadata comparisons passed.','MoE selected BN256/BK512/two TDM buffers, 256 resident CTAs, 297 VGPR/157152B LDS/0 spills; all8 random/collision fixtures bitwise match native.','No new end-to-end TTFT/TPOT/tokens/s run in this task. Existing serving path remains the previous saved version.'])
(r/'RESULTS.json').write_text(json.dumps(report,indent=2))
s=['# C8 AITER-guided region tuning — 2026-10-21','','Selected isolated single-launch regions. Four GPUs used. All µs are second-round medians per eight-token decode batch. Native is installed ATOM/AITER dispatch.','','| Group | Native µs (fresh) | Old fused µs | New fused µs | New vs native |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for d in rows:s.append(f"| {d['group']} | {d['native_us']:.2f} | {d['before_fused_us']:.2f} | {d['after_fused_us']:.2f} | {d['vs_native_pct']:+.1f}% |")
s+=['','## Selected changes','','- Attention: eight splits; row/head/split task interleaving across the resident grid; no empty-split stores; direct paged-cache TDM gathers and direct current-KV substitution. Bounded per-task TDM L2 prefetch retained. The separate 6–17 µs compact-cache copy is absent from this new region.','- mHC: inline AITER gfx1250 fused post/projection/squared-sum producer and original warp-specialized reduce/apply kernel in one launch. Dedicated producer subgroup barrier. Exact outputs in all16 tested fixtures.','- Routing: native-style parallel per-row topk; histogram/offset computation distributed across row CTAs rather than a serial CTA0 loop. 64 checks cover batches1/2/4/8, bias, and equal-score ties.','- MoE: match native K512/two-buffer pipeline; widen N128 to N256 for the fixed256 resident grid; use device-coherent load polling and actual active-expert task bounds. N512 and two/four persistent-N-tile variants were tested and rejected.','- HCA compressor: native-style K-parallel pooling, distributed across four CTAs per token; merge partial softmax statistics before norm/RoPE/cache write. Dedicated producer subgroup barriers.','- Indexer compressor: limit producer barrier to the32 producing CTAs; preserve sequential pooling arithmetic after parallel pooling regressed.','','## Remaining work','','Full-layer embedding and end-to-end validation are separate outstanding steps. Selected region ABIs/scratch need wiring; the serving kernel was not silently changed. The remaining >10% gaps are routed MoE, HCA boundary compression, and indexer boundary compression (CSA640 is approximately10%). Do not sum these ablations as full-layer latency.','','## Validation and limitations','']+['- '+x for x in report['limitations']]
(r/'RESULTS.md').write_text('\n'.join(s)+'\n')
manifest={str(p.relative_to(r)):hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in r.glob('*.py')};(r/'SOURCE_SHA256.json').write_text(json.dumps(manifest,indent=2))
print('\n'.join(s[:20]))
